EnhancedIRL Encoder image for the NVIDIA Jetson Nano Developer Kit

This system was put together by EnhancedIRL (https://github.com/enhanced-irl/eirl-encoder,
tools/image/ and IMAGE.md) from:

- Ubuntu 18.04 packages (arm64), installed as Ubuntu publishes them, with some of their
  configuration files changed (the system's name, the login messages, the services that run). The
  image is built from Ubuntu packages and is not Ubuntu: it is not affiliated with or endorsed by
  Canonical Ltd. Each package's licence is in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright; the texts of the
  common licences are in /usr/share/common-licenses.

- NVIDIA Jetson Linux (L4T) R32.7.6 for the Jetson Nano, as NVIDIA ships it. NVIDIA's proprietary
  software is under the NVIDIA Driver License Agreement, which is in
  /usr/share/doc/nvidia-tegra/L4T_End_User_License_Agreement.txt.gz, with the licences of its parts
  next to it; its open-source parts (the Linux kernel, U-Boot and others) keep their own licences,
  and SOURCES.md says where their source is. NVIDIA and Jetson are trademarks of NVIDIA
  Corporation; this image is not made, endorsed or supported by NVIDIA.

- Our kernel modules (tc358743, the cellular modem and the Bluetooth modules) and the board's
  device tree: GNU General Public License version 2. The Realtek RTL8761B Bluetooth firmware, from
  linux-firmware, redistributable under /lib/firmware/rtl_bt/LICENCE.rtlwifi_firmware.txt.

- The EnhancedIRL Encoder software: Apache License 2.0, with the third-party programs it carries;
  its notices and licences are in /usr/share/doc/eirl-encoder/.

Where the source code of all of it is, and our written offer for it: SOURCES.md, next to this file.
